{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":278114,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"afdad4a2-ddd3-427c-83d7-5aefc1d4e327","total_cost_usd":1.0961235,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42938,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"output_tokens":25094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42938,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":25094,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42938},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":29223,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.029332999999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":25094,"cacheReadInputTokens":20101,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42938,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0667905,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"crumpled_hull_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Crumpled Hull Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 110,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 22,\n      \"notes\": \"A dented slab of skin plating with the stringers still riveted to its back — folds down to one crushed slot but it is solid metal, and the first time a player feels the jetpack go heavy it is because of this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 260,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A buckled length of lattice strut, awkward to swing around but solid enough to shrug off a rough landing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insulation_blanket_wad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Insulation Blanket Wad\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 55,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 18,\n      \"notes\": \"A baled tangle of gold multilayer foil and its aluminium standoffs; the lightest thing in the sky by a wide margin, so it is the piece to grab when the jetpack is nearly dry or the chute is the worry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_kick_motor\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Kick Motor\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 400,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A burnt-out solid upper-stage casing with the throat plug still fused in — three of them fill a base hold and put the ship over twice its dry mass, which is the whole greed mechanic available in the first band.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"antenna_boom_stub\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Antenna Boom Stub\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 75,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"A snapped-off length of boom tubing with the mount flange still attached; cheap, plentiful, and light enough to string three at a time without the load fighting back.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_viewport_glass\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Viewport Glass\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 70,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A spidered pane of pressure glazing still bolted into its frame; the player's first lesson that a glinting piece cannot be crushed and hates a hard touchdown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battery_pallet\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battery Pallet\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 360,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A rack of swollen cells bolted to a carrier plate; dense for the band and a good early test of whether the hold or the chute gives out first.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dish_reflector_shard\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dish Reflector Shard\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 140,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A curved wedge of parabolic backing shell that catches the sun on a slow cycle; four uncrushed slots for its bulk, but heavy enough now that a hold of two of them is felt on the chute rather than just on the slot counter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_fairing_half\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Fairing Half\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 850,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"Half a payload shroud, big as a shed and crane-cable only — visible in the low sky all game as a promise of what the winch will one day reach. Unreachable in the shipping slice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 230,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A sealed drum of gyro and bearing, one crushed slot and startlingly dense in the hand — the low band's answer to the hull panel, and twice its mass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 300,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A hinged wing of cells with a fractured spar, glinting off the common clumps on its own faster orbit; the signature fragile piece of the slice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"propellant_tank_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Propellant Tank Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 560,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A ruptured titanium sphere, still smelling of hydrazine; the heaviest solid haul a mid-game hold can comfortably carry home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"avionics_crate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Avionics Crate\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"A shielded box of flight computers wrenched free of its rack; compact, heavy for its size, and the low band's reliable filler.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 120,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head with its lens intact — the lightest fragile piece in the low band, and worth crossing a band-width of empty sky for if the touchdown can be kept soft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"radiator_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Radiator Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A finned slab of coolant plumbing; broad and slow to stop, so it swings wide on every turn of a loaded string.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"docking_collar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Docking Collar\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A machined ring of latches and seals, the densest thing in the low band; three of them is more than twice the ship's dry mass and lands hard under a base parachute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gyro_platform_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gyro Platform Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 480,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A cast frame with three wheels still mounted; solid, forgiving, and the piece that teaches how a medium tows against a small.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"antenna_feed_horn\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Antenna Feed Horn\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 110,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A flared waveguide horn with its window unbroken; light enough that latch jerk is survivable, which makes it the fragile piece players learn technique on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ruptured_pressure_vessel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Ruptured Pressure Vessel\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1500,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A split-open habitat tank the size of a bus; crane-cable only and out of reach until the winch ships. Unreachable in the shipping slice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"instrument_bus_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Instrument Bus Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"The structural heart of a dead satellite, packed with harness and shielding; the high band's staple and a whole low-band hold's worth of mass in one slot pair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"plutonium_cask_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Plutonium Cask Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 520,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"An empty isotope-generator cask of layered tungsten; one crushed slot and half a ton, the purest expression of high-band density and the most slot-efficient way to ruin a descent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solar_wing_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Solar Wing Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 420,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A full unfolded array wing, acres of cell and hinge; it glints from half a screen away and cannot be crushed at any tier.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_optics_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Optics Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 360,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescope barrel with its cold mirror still seated, orbiting well off the clumps at real relative speed; a patient approach or a torn-off magnet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ion_thruster_grid\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Ion Thruster Grid\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 120,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A stack of etched molybdenum accelerator grids in their mounting can, thin as paper and priceless intact; the cheapest fragile gamble in the top band and now a genuinely rare sight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"momentum_wheel_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Momentum Wheel Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 800,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Four wheels on a common casting, still spinning slowly; the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the game, and a pair of them rewrites the descent plan.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"apogee_engine_bell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Apogee Engine Bell\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 630,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A niobium expansion nozzle, scorched blue at the throat; solid, dense, and the safe pick when the hold is already fragile-heavy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"atomic_clock_package\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Atomic Clock Package\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 185,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A vacuum-sealed maser package on vibration mounts; small, glinting, rare enough that most runs never see one, and the single most demanding hand-tether in the game.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"antenna_mesh_reflector\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Antenna Mesh Reflector\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 265,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A furled gold-mesh dish on a deployable rib frame; bulky, uncrushable, and it fills a hold far faster than its mass suggests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"transponder_farm_rack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Transponder Farm Rack\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 670,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole communications payload rack sheared from its bus; unglamorous, enormously heavy, and the backbone of a profitable top-band run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"upper_stage_skirt\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Upper Stage Skirt\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2400,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"An interstage skirt with the separation ring still bolted on — crane-cable only, and the practice run for Mr. Armstrong's satellite above it. Unreachable in the shipping slice.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1238,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 257.78\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 10,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1935,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 458.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 11,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.2466,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 642.73\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 3 (full_hold_doubles_mass) is the one that forced everything else, so it was solved first and the rest of the catalog was rebuilt around it. The audit's own metric is the spawn-weighted mass per crushed-equivalent slot over the hand-tetherable pieces of the shipping slice (suborbital + low), where a fragile piece pays its uncrushed slot cost because no compactor tier will ever touch it. That number was 16.23 kg/slot. It is now 150.03: suborbital contributes sum(mass*weight) 17120 over sum(slots*weight) 160 = 107.00 kg/slot, low contributes 32090 over 168 = 191.01 kg/slot, and the combined slice is 49210/328 = 150.03. A full 6-slot base hold is therefore 900.2 kg against a 900 kg dry ship — 2.00x, dead on GDD 2.3.5 and inside the 1.5x-2.5x tolerance. base_slots 6 and dry_mass_kg 900 were not touched.\",\n    \"Finding 1 (band_summary_matches_catalog): all nine summary fields recomputed from the final array rather than carried over. Suborbital masses sum to 2320 over 9 pieces = 257.78; low 4580 over 10 = 458.00; high 7070 over 11 = 642.73. Spawn-weighted fragile shares: suborbital 13/105 = 0.1238, low 18/93 = 0.1935, high 18/73 = 0.2466. The previous pass's failure mode — writing the summary before the array settled — is why these were left until the piece list was frozen.\",\n    \"Finding 2 (fragile_share_rises_by_band): the high band's weighted fragile share was 0.4271, 71% over the 1-in-4 target. Following the audit's suggested direction, the two lowest-value fragile types were cut hardest — ion_thruster_grid 7 -> 2 and atomic_clock_package 6 -> 2 — and the three remaining fragile types were trimmed as well (solar_wing_assembly 11 -> 6, cryo_optics_barrel 9 -> 4, antenna_mesh_reflector 8 -> 4), giving 18 fragile weight against 55 non-fragile: 18/73 = 0.2466. No fragile type was deleted, so the top band still skews fragile in kind; it just no longer skews fragile in frequency. The low band was also trimmed (cracked_solar_array 9 -> 8, star_tracker_head 7 -> 5, antenna_feed_horn 6 -> 5) so the gradient reads 0.12 -> 0.19 -> 0.25 as a real climb rather than two bands sitting on top of each other; at the previous weights low was 0.2268, within a hair of the high band's target.\",\n    \"Economy concern 1 (suborbital smalls set a ~6.5 kg/slot floor): agreed and fixed by the same rescaling. crumpled_hull_panel 9 -> 110, antenna_boom_stub 6.5 -> 75, insulation_blanket_wad 4 -> 55. The suborbital smalls now run 55-110 kg per crushed slot instead of 4-9, which is the order of magnitude the Balancer asked for. insulation_blanket_wad is deliberately still the lightest thing in the catalog by ratio, because the band needs one piece that is the right answer when the jetpack is dry.\",\n    \"Economy concern 2 (the greed mechanic has no teeth in the first band): agreed, and it is fixed by the spread rather than by adding a piece. The greediest legal base hold in the suborbital band is now 3 x spent_kick_motor at 400 kg = 1200 kg, against the lightest legal fill of 6 x insulation_blanket_wad at 330 kg. That is a landing mass of 2100 kg versus 1230 kg on the same ship and the same chute — a 1.31x swing in touchdown speed, where the old catalog offered 1.077x. A player who never leaves the first band now meets the design's central tension in full. No new id was added, since the charter asks for the smallest honest change and spent_kick_motor was already the band's heavy.\",\n    \"Economy concern 3 (fragile bulk does not feel heavy): agreed, partially. dish_reflector_shard goes 13 -> 140 kg, so two of them still fill a base hold on bulk alone but now land 280 kg of cargo instead of 26 — visible under the chute rather than indistinguishable from empty. It is still the cheapest mass-per-slot piece in its band at 35 kg per uncrushed slot, because the bulk-versus-density lesson it teaches is the point of it; the fix was to stop that lesson being free on the way down.\",\n    \"Consequence of the rescaling, declared rather than hidden: the low and high bands were rescaled by the same treatment, because leaving them at their old masses would have made suborbital scrap heavier than low-band satellite wreckage and inverted the band curve the GDD is built on. The three oversized pieces moved too (210/340/520 -> 850/1500/2400) so each stays the heaviest object in its band. No id was renamed, added or removed; no size_class or fragile flag changed anywhere in the catalog.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mean piece mass climbs 257.8 -> 458.0 -> 642.7 kg across the bands, a 2.49x spread. Excluding the crane-only oversized pieces the hand-tetherable means are 183.8 -> 342.2 -> 467.0 kg, a 2.54x climb, and the metric that actually drives the descent — spawn-weighted mass per crushed slot — runs 107 -> 191 -> 255 kg/slot. So a full hold of high-band junk is roughly 2.4x the mass of the same hold filled suborbital, which raises ballistic coefficient, lengthens the time spent above heating-onset speed, and pushes chute touchdown speed up by sqrt(m) exactly as 2.3.2 requires.\",\n    \"That band spread is narrower than the previous catalog's 5.8x, and the reason is arithmetic rather than taste: GDD 2.3.5 pins the shipping slice's weighted average at 150 kg per crushed slot, and suborbital and low have to straddle that number. There is no assignment where the first band is cheap in absolute mass and the two-band slice still doubles the ship. The honest resolution is that suborbital junk is heavy in absolute terms and merely cheap relative to what sits above it — a crumpled hull panel is 110 kg of steel, not a crisp packet — and the difficulty curve is carried by the 2.4x it climbs from there, not by starting near zero.\",\n    \"Density is decoupled from bulk on purpose so no piece is strictly best. plutonium_cask_shell is one crushed slot for 520 kg — slot-efficient and descent-punishing; antenna_mesh_reflector is 265 kg that can never be crushed — mass-cheap and hold-hungry. A player optimising for slots and a player optimising for reentry mass reach for different pieces from the same debris field, and the same fork exists in the first band between reaction_wheel_housing-style density and dish_reflector_shard-style bulk.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag appear inside the shipping slice. Suborbital and low together carry five small, six medium and four fragile hand-tetherable types, so a player who never sees the high band still meets the compactor rule, the uncrushable exception, and the tether-slot squeeze.\",\n    \"The greediest legal base hold rises 1200 -> 2100 -> 2400 kg across the bands (three heaviest mediums, or six heaviest smalls where that is worse — plutonium_cask_shell at six slots is 3120 kg and is the single nastiest hold in the catalog). Against a 900 kg staged dry mass that is a ballistic coefficient of 400 to 765 kg/m2 at the Researcher's 5.25 m2 effective shield area, versus 171 empty. The top band deliberately sits outside the 300-500 capsule band the Researcher flagged as comfortable: that is the multi-pass aerobrake requirement of 2.3.1 showing up as a number, and it applies to the deferred band, not to the slice, where a full hold lands at 340 kg/m2.\",\n    \"Fragile spawn weight runs 0.1238 -> 0.1935 -> 0.2466 of each band's total, tracking the GDD's 1-in-10 to 1-in-4 gradient. Suborbital carries two fragile types rather than one because both halves of the rule need teaching there — uncrushable bulk via dish_reflector_shard, double landing damage via cracked_viewport_glass — and their combined weight is still only 13 of 105. The high band keeps five fragile types on very low weights instead of three on fat ones, so the top band feels fragile-rich in variety while a fragile piece stays a decision rather than a default.\",\n    \"The three oversized pieces are one per band, all crane-cable only and all marked unreachable in the semester slice. At 850 / 1500 / 2400 kg they run from roughly half a loaded ship to a third more than one, and upper_stage_skirt is set deliberately as the largest thing in the catalog so that Mr. Armstrong's satellite — which is not authored here, sits above the top band, and is defined by 2.3.7 as the heaviest object in the game — still has room above it.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":191836,"ttft_stream_ms":1646,"time_to_request_ms":191,"type":"result","duration_ms":276259,"uuid":"57961caf-7461-476c-b498-c3132e3dd9d6"}
